      "license": "GPL-3.0-only",
      "changes": "Hushfacebook's TapClock and the decision core of TapToPlay, packages moved from app.morphe.extension.facebook to app.hushgram.extension.instagram. Instagram's starts carry a reason string instead of Facebook's EventTriggerType, and it can't tell a tap from an automatic start, so the control triggers and the visibility triggers went: a start goes ahead on an armed player or within a second of a tap. The legacy player, the Reels play button and overlay hooks went with them. The Autoplay setting reader became a boolean filter on Instagram's VideoAutoplayChecker, and the pause hook takes Instagram's pause reason so a seek, a pinch or a reel's replay keeps the player armed. ResumePoints came over as it was. ResumePlayback kept the thresholds and the player bookkeeping, and reads Instagram's IgVideoPlayerImpl and IgVideoSource through stubs the patch fills, where it read Facebook's VideoPlayerParams by field name. Long reels resume, since Instagram posts nearly every video as a reel. The trigger enum, the release hook and the loop, GIF and audio-only checks went, and Instagram's first video start ages the saved points instead of Facebook's app start. The tests were ported with them. TapToPlay also hands the feed's Litho play button to HushGram's own PlayButtons, which hides it while the video a tap on it started plays, and lets a tap's first start come up to four seconds after it, for a story that's slow to load. TapClock also keeps how long a tap was held, and TapToPlay remembers the players it held, so the release of a press and hold on a held story takes the story player's resume. Changed files carry a 'Modified for HushGram' line."
    },
